data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Find the binade of |x| from its exponent. The spacing in that binade is 2**(max(exp, e_min) - m), where\ne_min = 1 - bias. Divide |x| by the spacing, round to the nearest integer with ties to even, and multiply\nback. A result above the largest finite value is an overflow to infinity. The largest finite value is\n(2 - 2**-m) * 2**(e_max) with e_max = 2**e - 2 - bias."},"hints_note":null}

