data: {"level":3,"reviewed":{"level":3,"label":"code shape","text":"Handle NaN, the infinities and zero first. For a normal value, get the binade exponent with\n`math.frexp`. Take the spacing with `math.ldexp`. Use Python's `round` on the quotient, which breaks\nties to even, then multiply back. Finish with `math.copysign` so the sign survives, and return an infinity\nwhen the rounded value passes the largest finite value."},"hints_note":null}

